{"name":"Earth Friendly","hex":"#c6ba92","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"earth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Earth (“the third planet of the Solar System, upon which humans live”)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Soil.","Any general rock-based material."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earth"},{"term":"friendly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Generally warm, approachable and easy to relate with in character.","Inviting, characteristic of friendliness."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A game which is of no consequence in terms of ranking, betting, etc.","A person or entity on the same side as one's own in a conflict."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friendly"}],"entries":[{"title":"Environmentally friendly process","blocks":[{"text":"Environmentally friendly processes – also called environment-friendly, eco-friendly, nature-friendly, or green processes – are a set of sustainability and marketing terms referring to goods and services, laws, guidelines, and policies that claim to reduce, minimize, or eliminate harm to ecosystems or the environment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Depuradora_de_Lluc.JPG/330px-Depuradora_de_Lluc.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Environmentally_friendly_process"},{"title":"Earth","blocks":[{"text":"Earth is the third planet from the Sun and the only astronomical object known to harbor life. This is made possible by Earth being an ocean world, the only one in the Solar System sustaining liquid surface water. Almost all of Earth's water is contained in its ocean, which covers 70.8% of Earth's crust. The remaining 29.2% of Earth's crust is dry land, which is predominantly located within Earth's land hemisphere in the form of continental landmasses. Most of Earth's land is at least somewhat humid and covered by vegetation, while large ice sheets at Earth's polar deserts retain more water than Earth's groundwater, lakes, rivers, and atmospheric water combined. Earth's crust consists of slowly moving tectonic plates, which interact to produce mountain ranges, volcanoes, and earthquakes. Earth has a liquid outer core that generates a magnetosphere capable of deflecting most of the destructive solar winds and cosmic radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Meteosat-12-fci-march-equinox-2025-noon.jpg/330px-Meteosat-12-fci-march-equinox-2025-noon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/%27Environmentally_Friendly%27_Speed_Warning_-_geograph.org.uk_-_49267.jpg/500px-%27Environmentally_Friendly%27_Speed_Warning_-_geograph.org.uk_-_49267.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/%27Environmentally_Friendly%27_Speed_Warning_-_geograph.org.uk_-_49267.jpg/500px-%27Environmentally_Friendly%27_Speed_Warning_-_geograph.org.uk_-_49267.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Environmentally friendly speed warning powered by solar and wind power.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A'Environmentally_Friendly'_Speed_Warning_-_geograph.org.uk_-_49267.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Beech_Forest_%28AU%29%2C_Great_Otway_National_Park%2C_Beauchamp_Falls_--_2019_--_1271.jpg/500px-Beech_Forest_%28AU%29%2C_Great_Otway_National_Park%2C_Beauchamp_Falls_--_2019_--_1271.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Beech_Forest_%28AU%29%2C_Great_Otway_National_Park%2C_Beauchamp_Falls_--_2019_--_1271.jpg/1280px-Beec